            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Tamil for to sing a lullaby, then the Tamil for to feed."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: கர்ப்பம்",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "கர்ப்பம் — karppam — \"pregnancy\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "என் அக்கா இப்போது ஆறு மாதக் கர்ப்பமாக இருக்கிறாள். eṉ akkā ippōtu āṟu mātak karppamāka irukkiṟāḷ. My elder sister is six months pregnant now."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "கர்ப்பமாக இரு, to be pregnant."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "கர்ப்பம் (karppam) is borrowed from Sanskrit garbha, \"womb, foetus\" (CDIAL 4055); Tamil writes the g and bh with க and ப."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for describing what you lived and felt."
            }
          ]
        },
